What is a Delay Condom?
A delay condom is a medical device that extends sexual intercourse by incorporating a mild desensitising agent into the latex or silicone layer. The agent, typically benzocaine or lidocaine, is calibrated to reduce penile sensitivity gradually, thereby prolonging the duration of sexual activity while maintaining contraceptive efficacy. Delay condoms are available in medical grade formulations that meet stringent safety and efficacy standards, as well as in non medical variants aimed at the broader consumer market where a lower concentration of desensitising agent is used.
This market segment combines the protective functionality of standard condoms with the performance enhancement sought by consumers who wish to extend the pleasure of intercourse. The product’s dual nature creates a unique positioning that intersects traditional contraceptive markets, sexual wellness initiatives, and lifestyle consumer segments.
